WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:12.603
"What you think of Tom Sawyer?"

2
00:00:12.984 --> 00:00:14.205
asked a reporter from a St.

3
00:00:14.245 --> 00:00:15.065
Louis newspaper.

4
00:00:15.966 --> 00:00:18.908
"He's a rascal," said the older woman sharply.

5
00:00:18.928 --> 00:00:23.612
"Finding that gold was just was just so unfortunate."

6
00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:26.695
"Ma'am, don't you mean 'fortunate?'"

7
00:00:27.095 --> 00:00:28.696
asked the reporter confused.

8
00:00:28.716 --> 00:00:33.884
"No, I mean unfortunate," said the woman.

9
00:00:33.904 --> 00:00:38.846
"It's unfortunate that such a mischievous boy found the gold."

10
00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:46.048
The reporter had interviewed ten different people about Tom Sawyer, and she had gotten ten different descriptions of

11
00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:47.028
the same boy.

12
00:00:48.029 --> 00:00:50.369
She truly did not understand what was going on.

13
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.651
What the reporter didn't know was that Tom Sawyer was not a single boy at all.

14
00:00:56.691 --> 00:01:01.877
His character was based on a collection of boys—boys who Samuel Clemens had known when he was growing

15
00:01:01.957 --> 00:01:03.198
up in Hannibal, Missouri.

16
00:01:04.658 --> 00:01:10.040
Samuel Clemens is best known as Mark Twain, the author of The Adventures of Tom Sawyer and The

17
00:01:10.081 --> 00:01:11.561
Adventures of Huckleberry Finn.

18
00:01:13.362 --> 00:01:17.764
If the reporter had asked Mark Twain about Tom Sawyer, she would have learned that Tom is a

19
00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:19.885
smart boy, but not "book smart."

20
00:01:21.005 --> 00:01:23.846
She would have learned that Tom is a good boy, but not "church good."

21
00:01:24.927 --> 00:01:29.381
In other words Tom is a completely ordinary child, except for his adventures.

22
00:01:30.462 --> 00:01:32.944
Tom's parents are dead, and Tom is an orphan.

23
00:01:33.905 --> 00:01:36.627
His mother's sister, Polly, has taken him into her house.

24
00:01:38.168 --> 00:01:41.111
Tom's world is the fictional town called Petersburg, Missouri.

25
00:01:42.031 --> 00:01:46.895
Most of Tom's friends lead fairly normal lives, with the exception, of course, of Huckleberry Finn.

26
00:01:47.976 --> 00:01:50.258
Huck, as he is called, is the son of a drunk.

27
00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:55.762
Tom, however, sees Huck as a friend who has all the luck—a boy who doesn't have to go

28
00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.304
to either school or church!

29
00:01:59.524 --> 00:02:02.606
Tom meets a new girl in town named Becky and wins her affection.

30
00:02:03.806 --> 00:02:07.708
She wins Tom's heart too, and some of his adventures happen because of her.

31
00:02:08.889 --> 00:02:11.250
She brings out a sensitive side of mischievous Tom.

32
00:02:12.971 --> 00:02:15.553
Mark Twain's novel is a classic story about a boy.

33
00:02:16.513 --> 00:02:21.336
Tom's youth, independence, and bright curiosity still charm many readers today.
